claim.claim-text:
forming a solar cell string (1) by sequentially connecting a plurality of solar cells (20), wherein light-receiving surfaces of adjacent solar cells (20) of the plurality of solar cells (20) face opposite directions, and forming the solar cell string (1) comprises:
providing a first adhesive layer (21);
placing the plurality of solar cells (20) on the first adhesive layer (21);
laying a plurality of second wires (22) between the first adhesive layer (21) and the plurality of solar cells (20) before placing the plurality of solar cells (20) on the first adhesive layer (21), wherein the plurality of second wires (22) are stretched to achieve series connection of the plurality of solar cells (20);
laying a plurality of first wires (23) on the plurality of solar cells (20) away from the first adhesive layer (21), wherein the plurality of first wires (23) are stretched to achieve series connection of the plurality of solar cells (20);
disposing a second adhesive layer (24) on a surface of the plurality of solar cells (20) away from the first adhesive layer (21), wherein the plurality of first wires (23) are located between the second adhesive layer (24) and the plurality of solar cells; and
performing a pressing treatment to bond and fix the first adhesive layer (21), the plurality of first wires (23), the plurality of second wires (22), the plurality of solar cells (20), and the second adhesive layer (24);

the first substrate (171) is a flexible or rigid substrate with high light transmittance or high reflectance;
the second substrate (172) is made of at least one of polyethylene terephthalate, tempered glass, and ethylene-tetrafluoroethylene copolymer;
the first encapsulating layer (161) is made of at least one of polyethylene-polyvinyl acetate copolymer, polyolefin, and polyvinyl butyral; and
the second encapsulating layer (162) is made of at least one of polyethylene-polyvinyl acetate copolymer, polyolefin, and polyvinyl butyral.
